      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Your patient's profile (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) doesn't call for a higher dose. A dose this high raises the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose. I can titrate to 10 mg later.\n3. **Amlodipine 30 mg as written**, if you intend it. Please confirm the dose is deliberate, and I can add a note to the order.\n\nI can also enter a different regimen, such as adding a second antihypertensive agent, if the goal is more blood pressure control than amlodipine 10 mg gives."
      }
     ],
